summary:
  parseFeed hands a guid-less episode the enclosure URL as its guid, so no feed
  is ever guid-less and the branch that handles rotating addresses is dead code.

history:
  episodeKey() already falls back to the url when the guid is empty, so the
  substitution in the parser bought nothing and cost the one fact the seen-key
  road asks for: does this show have stable ids. A feed whose media URLs carry
  a rotating token then changed its "guid" on every fetch, the newest-episode
  key changed with it, and each poll announced the same episode as new — one
  extra download per cycle. The guid-less branch in PodcastEngine
  (seenKeyOf -> legacy title name) was written for exactly this and could never
  run. Found 2026-09-18 while re-checking a round-5 refutation that had closed
  only half the claim.

target:
  package/contents/ui/PodcastLogic.js

find:
      guid: guid,

replace:
      guid: guid !== "" ? guid : url,

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_podcastlogic.qml::test_a_feed_without_guids_says_so
  (and test_realistic_feed_parses_the_survivors). Line-neutral.
